<name><surname>Lepage</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>d'Agay</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Briere</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lavignac</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Fillet</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Salles</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Marolleau</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Diebold</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Reyas</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaulard</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prognostic significance of bcl-2 protein expression in aggressive non-Hodgkin's lymphoma. Groupe d'Etude des Lymphomes de l'Adulte (GELA)</article-title><source>Blood</source><year>1996</year><volume>87</volume><fpage>265</fpage><lpage>272</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Blood||87|265||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8547651</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Homma</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Furuta</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Oridate</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakano</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kohashi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Yagi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Nagahashi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Fukuda</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Inoue</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Inuyama</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prognostic significance of clinical parameters and biological markers in patients with squamous cell carcinoma of the head and neck treated with concurrent che